{"name":"Astronomer","hex":"#e8f2eb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"astronomer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who studies astronomy, the stars or the physical universe; a scientist whose area of research is astronomy or astrophysics."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astronomer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Astronomer","blocks":[{"text":"An astronomer is a scientist in the field of astronomy who focuses on a specific question or field outside the scope of Earth. Astronomers study astronomical objects, such as stars, planets, moons, comets and galaxies, by some combination of observation and the application of astrophysical models. Examples of topics or fields astronomers study include planetary science, solar astronomy, the origin or evolution of stars, or the formation of galaxies. A related but distinct subject is physical cosmology, which studies the universe as a whole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/IAU_2006_General_Assembly-_Result_of_the_IAU_Resolution_Votes_%28iau0603g%29.jpg/330px-IAU_2006_General_Assembly-_Result_of_the_IAU_Resolution_Votes_%28iau0603g%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronomer","wikidata":"Q11063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei_%28Uffizi%29.jpg/500px-Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei_%28Uffizi%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei_%28Uffizi%29.jpg/1280px-Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei_%28Uffizi%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei_%28Uffizi%29